{"v":1,"accession":"PRJDB45648","title":"Alzheimer's Disease Promotion by Ambient Fine Particulate Matter (PRJCA060651)","description":"This study investigates the causal mechanisms linking fine particulate matter (PM2.5) exposure to Alzheimer's disease (AD) pathogenesis via the gut-brain axis. Mechanistically, utilizing a real-world PM2.5 exposure 5xFAD mouse model, we demonstrate that PM2.5 accelerates cognitive impairment and β-amyloid deposition in a sex-dependent and disease-stage-specific manner. Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) experiments confirm the mediating role of gut microbiota in PM2.5-induced neurotoxicity. Integrative multi-omics analysis of gut microbiota-derived extracellular vesicles (GMEVs) metaproteomics and brain spatial transcriptomics reveals that PM2.5-induced dysbiosis alters GMEV protein cargo, which targets astrocytic and neuronal populations in the hippocampus to promote amyloid-beta deposition and disrupt neural circuits. This research provides novel evidence for the early prevention of AD by elucidating how environmental pollutants trigger neuroimmune dysregulation through the microbiota-gut-brain axis.","center":"Fudan University","data_type":"Other","submission_date":"2026/10/28 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMD01984294","AD3-198 (SAMC7358465)","non_environmental",null,"2023-02-17",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"missing: data agreement established pre-2023",null,null,null,null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMD01984295","AD3-187 (SAMC7358466)","non_environmental",null,"2023-02-17",2023,null,null,null,null,"unresolved",null,null,"missing: data agreement established pre-2023",null,null,null,null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMD01984296","A